# Line endings are load-bearing for two kinds of file in this repository.
#
# docker-entrypoint.sh MUST be LF. A CRLF version fails at container start with
# "/bin/sh: 1: ...: \r: not found", because the carriage return becomes part of
# the command. That is an opaque failure on a machine where everything else looks
# correct, and it only appears on Windows checkouts — which is where the commit
# was made.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Dockerfile and the YAML Render reads are not shell, but CRLF in a Dockerfile
# produces a stray \r in COPY paths on some builders. Cheap to pin.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
render.yaml text eol=lf

# SQL is loaded by MySQL's SOURCE, which tolerates CRLF, but pinning it keeps
# the files byte-identical between a Windows and a Linux checkout so a diff of
# the schema is only ever a real change.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Everything else: let the repo's existing behaviour stand.
* text=auto
